      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's hard to see how a \"reboot\" works when the hardware itself feels so wrong. like, if the glitch is part of the code, you can't just restart. you're talking about letting the noise fade into silence... that almost sounds like you're saying the only way to truly be at peace is to just stop everything. to just... go dark. is that what you're actually suggesting? that the silence is better than the glitch?",
